WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.132
- Good morning Believe Nation!

00:00:01.132 --> 00:00:04.068
My name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is believe,

00:00:04.068 --> 00:00:06.085
and I believe that entrepreneurs are going

00:00:06.085 --> 00:00:09.338
to solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:10.822
So, to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.822 --> 00:00:13.705
today we're going to learn how to commit.

00:00:13.705 --> 00:00:15.660
Over to you Vince Lombardi.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.010
(rooster crowing)

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.867
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:23.414
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:23.414 --> 00:00:27.458
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:27.458 --> 00:00:31.625
- I've been around high
performance people all my life.

00:00:32.986 --> 00:00:36.918
And really for my own
growth, my own development,

00:00:36.918 --> 00:00:41.085
I've made it my mission, my
purpose, to study these people.

00:00:43.406 --> 00:00:44.636
People of all walks of life.

00:00:44.636 --> 00:00:48.126
People of military. People in government.

00:00:48.126 --> 00:00:51.043
Word class athletes. Great coaches.

00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:56.306
People of the private
sector, such as a lot of you.

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:59.452
And I've studied them with a thought.

00:00:59.452 --> 00:01:03.035
What do they do when
they're at their best?

00:01:04.421 --> 00:01:09.245
It's my intention this evening
to hold up for you a mirror.

00:01:09.245 --> 00:01:10.419
A mirror that you can look into

00:01:10.419 --> 00:01:12.800
and examine for yourself the breadth

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.584
and the depth of your
goals, and the commitment,

00:01:15.584 --> 00:01:18.765
and the discipline, and
the perseverance you bring

00:01:18.765 --> 00:01:21.265
to the pursuit of those goals.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.740
It's my intention this evening

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.715
to curate within you a little dissidence,

00:01:27.715 --> 00:01:30.586
a little disharmony, a
little dissatisfaction,

00:01:30.586 --> 00:01:33.503
which is the essence of motivation.

00:01:35.478 --> 00:01:37.418
So of the balance of the evening you begin

00:01:37.418 --> 00:01:41.120
to ask yourself some hard questions.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.889
And maybe you'll be
satisfied with the answers,

00:01:44.889 --> 00:01:46.556
and maybe you won't.

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:53.993
I'm not going to tell you
anything you don't already know.

00:01:53.993 --> 00:01:54.826
Just thought that maybe I'd present it

00:01:54.826 --> 00:01:57.394
to you a little differently.

00:01:57.394 --> 00:02:02.328
Perhaps in a manner that you
haven't seen or heard before.

00:02:02.328 --> 00:02:03.166
Now you may sit there and say,

00:02:03.166 --> 00:02:06.083
"Well, Vince. Nothing new. Come on.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.023
Not the same old, same old.

00:02:11.023 --> 00:02:12.831
Not the same old motivational stuff

00:02:12.831 --> 00:02:16.914
where every time we come
to a meeting like this."

00:02:18.773 --> 00:02:21.598
Well, let me ask you a question.

00:02:21.598 --> 00:02:23.069
How many diets does it take to get down

00:02:23.069 --> 00:02:26.136
to the weight you'd like to be at?

00:02:26.136 --> 00:02:28.886
Just one. The one you stick with.

00:02:31.237 --> 00:02:33.434
How many times you have
to reorganize your office,

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:36.570
your desk, your approach to
your business, your profession,

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.328
your career before you begin to see some

00:02:38.328 --> 00:02:41.078
of the results you'd like to see?

00:02:42.368 --> 00:02:46.285
Just one. The one you
commit to and stick with.

00:02:49.201 --> 00:02:51.512
And how many personal growth programs

00:02:51.512 --> 00:02:54.104
do you have to take on before you begin

00:02:54.104 --> 00:02:55.287
to see some of the changes

00:02:55.287 --> 00:02:59.454
in your personal life you'd
like to see? Just one.

00:03:02.157 --> 00:03:06.607
The one you commit to and
discipline yourself to stick with.

00:03:06.607 --> 00:03:08.508
- Most people don't get the
success that they're looking for

00:03:08.508 --> 00:03:10.900
because they don't
commit to doing the work.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.184
Again, if you look at any
major successful person

00:03:13.184 --> 00:03:14.563
that you look up to in any field,

00:03:14.563 --> 00:03:16.202
the people who are your role models,

00:03:16.202 --> 00:03:18.680
the people you want to emulate,
the people you want to be like.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.323
They got there because
they committed to the plan.

00:03:21.323 --> 00:03:24.711
They took action every
single day on that plan.

00:03:24.711 --> 00:03:27.948
Too many people get started on one thing,

00:03:27.948 --> 00:03:30.651
and they lose interest in
it, or it starts to get hard,

00:03:30.651 --> 00:03:31.667
and so they jump to another thing,

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:32.500
and they jump to another thing,

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.666
and they jump to another thing.

00:03:33.666 --> 00:03:35.855
And because they don't
take consistent action,

00:03:35.855 --> 00:03:38.148
because they don't
commit fully to the plan,

00:03:38.148 --> 00:03:41.006
then they don't have the
success that they want to have.

00:03:41.006 --> 00:03:44.628
Because anything that is worth
doing is going to get hard.

00:03:44.628 --> 00:03:47.055
Starting a business is really hard.

00:03:47.055 --> 00:03:48.617
Losing weight is hard.

00:03:48.617 --> 00:03:49.893
Putting on muscle is hard.

00:03:49.893 --> 00:03:52.738
All the important things that
you want to go after and do,

00:03:52.738 --> 00:03:55.621
at some point, is going to get hard.

00:03:55.621 --> 00:03:58.496
And what most people do,
as soon as it gets hard,

00:03:58.496 --> 00:04:00.379
is they quit and they go look

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:02.313
for a shortcut down another path,

00:04:02.313 --> 00:04:04.314
because that path is
going to be way easier

00:04:04.314 --> 00:04:05.638
than what you're doing right now.

00:04:05.638 --> 00:04:08.328
As soon as that path gets
hard, you jump to another path,

00:04:08.328 --> 00:04:10.309
which is also, you think
is going to be easier,

00:04:10.309 --> 00:04:12.501
but as soon as it gets hard, you stop.

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:14.414
And that's what most
people do with businesses.

00:04:14.414 --> 00:04:15.850
They start a business. It gets hard.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:16.964
They go do something else. It gets hard.

00:04:16.964 --> 00:04:17.921
They go do something else.

00:04:17.921 --> 00:04:19.545
It's what they do with diets.

00:04:19.545 --> 00:04:21.507
They start a diet. It gets too hard.

00:04:21.507 --> 00:04:23.415
That didn't work. They gave it two days.

00:04:23.415 --> 00:04:24.653
It didn't work. They gave it a week.

00:04:24.653 --> 00:04:27.211
It didn't work. They quit and
they go do something else.

00:04:27.211 --> 00:04:30.072
It doesn't matter which diet you stick to.

00:04:30.072 --> 00:04:32.804
For the business, as long as
you're passionate about it.

00:04:32.804 --> 00:04:34.668
The one that's going to work is the one

00:04:34.668 --> 00:04:38.946
that you commit to and take
daily consistent action on.

00:04:38.946 --> 00:04:41.692
If I look at my YouTube
channel, it started to explode

00:04:41.692 --> 00:04:44.692
and really grow when I
committed to it more fully.

00:04:44.692 --> 00:04:48.442
At the start, I just had a
channel, I just saved the name.

00:04:48.442 --> 00:04:51.231
I was posting a couple videos,
answering some questions,

00:04:51.231 --> 00:04:53.103
but it wasn't until I
took it consistently,

00:04:53.103 --> 00:04:55.996
when I said, "Okay, I'm
going to do regular videos

00:04:55.996 --> 00:04:57.763
from once a week, to once a day,

00:04:57.763 --> 00:05:00.359
to twice a day, to three times a day."

00:05:00.359 --> 00:05:01.600
Go back on my channel,

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.276
and that's when you see the
growth starts to happen.

00:05:04.276 --> 00:05:07.008
And that's going to happen
in every area of your life.

00:05:07.008 --> 00:05:08.316
In every business decision.

00:05:08.316 --> 00:05:09.783
In every personal decision.

00:05:09.783 --> 00:05:12.189
When you commit to following through,

00:05:12.189 --> 00:05:14.173
and you take consistent action on it,

00:05:14.173 --> 00:05:16.524
that's when you start to see results.

00:05:16.524 --> 00:05:18.324
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious,

00:05:18.324 --> 00:05:21.424
what are you afraid to commit to?

00:05:21.424 --> 00:05:23.601
In your business, or in your life.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:25.307
What's almost there, but you're afraid

00:05:25.307 --> 00:05:28.060
to take that final step
and go all in and commit.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.265
Leave it in the comments below.

00:05:29.265 --> 00:05:30.683
I'm super curious to find out.

00:05:30.683 --> 00:05:32.838
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to Xavier Monty

00:05:32.838 --> 00:05:34.857
from hellotalent.com.

00:05:34.857 --> 00:05:36.559
Xavier, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:05:36.559 --> 00:05:38.464
of my book, 'Your One Word.'

00:05:38.464 --> 00:05:40.351
I really appreciate the support, man,

00:05:40.351 --> 00:05:42.539
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:05:42.539 --> 00:05:43.992
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:43.992 --> 00:05:45.097
I believe in you.

00:05:45.097 --> 00:05:47.175
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:05:47.175 --> 00:05:50.348
and whatever your one word is, much love,

00:05:50.348 --> 00:05:51.757
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:51.757 --> 00:05:54.530
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:57.270
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:00.853
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:06:03.706 --> 00:06:05.865
- I looked at the odds, you know,

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:10.420
like how am I even going to
break in to this business, right.

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:13.540
All the good parts, you know.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:16.957
As an unknown actor, to get a great role,

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:21.323
every other actor has
to pass on it, right.

00:06:21.323 --> 00:06:23.331
Every other actor has to pass on it.

00:06:23.331 --> 00:06:26.149
And then it gets opened up to you

00:06:26.149 --> 00:06:29.780
and thousands of other
people like you, right,

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.501
and you all go.

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:33.668
And there are a few parts.

00:06:34.601 --> 00:06:37.095
Like I was looking at a big part

00:06:37.095 --> 00:06:40.095
when I was younger, was Primal Fear.

00:06:42.224 --> 00:06:43.650
Remember that movie with Richard Gere?

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:46.671
And Edward Norton got the part.

00:06:46.671 --> 00:06:48.666
- [Interviewer] After everyone passed.

00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:51.958
- Yeah. So that part became
open, every young actor knew it.

00:06:51.958 --> 00:06:54.765
I mean we went, I paid
with money I did not have

00:06:54.765 --> 00:06:56.765
to take dialect lessons.

00:06:58.062 --> 00:07:00.622
Hired a dialect coach because the kid was,

00:07:00.622 --> 00:07:02.179
his alter ego was from Kentucky,

00:07:02.179 --> 00:07:03.014
and he was from somewhere else,

00:07:03.014 --> 00:07:05.597
and I'd never been to Kentucky.

00:07:06.868 --> 00:07:08.564
We knew that that was it.

00:07:08.564 --> 00:07:11.147
That was going to launch somebody.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:15.219
There just weren't opportunities.

00:07:15.219 --> 00:07:17.345
And so Courage Under Fire was one

00:07:17.345 --> 00:07:19.027
of those roles that was small.

00:07:19.027 --> 00:07:22.369
It was really only, it was two scenes.

00:07:22.369 --> 00:07:24.144
I had two scenes with Denzel.

00:07:24.144 --> 00:07:27.727
And then the rest of
it was, I'm the medic.

00:07:29.443 --> 00:07:30.966
Tim Guinee, an actor who I love,

00:07:30.966 --> 00:07:32.991
who's in Promised Land, actually,

00:07:32.991 --> 00:07:35.523
is like bleeding out on my lap.

00:07:35.523 --> 00:07:38.031
For six weeks we're in El Paso,

00:07:38.031 --> 00:07:39.787
and he's moaning, and
I'm just sitting there,

00:07:39.787 --> 00:07:41.609
and I'm like, "I don't think
the camera's on us man."

00:07:41.609 --> 00:07:43.859
(laughing)

00:07:47.583 --> 00:07:51.250
It was a really thankless
job for both of us

00:07:52.374 --> 00:07:55.653
except for those two scenes
that I had with Denzel.

00:07:55.653 --> 00:07:57.668
So I had two days of work on that movie,

00:07:57.668 --> 00:08:00.243
and so I went, well, what do I do?

00:08:00.243 --> 00:08:02.502
It's told in flashback, so let me see.

00:08:02.502 --> 00:08:04.502
How can I change myself?

00:08:05.781 --> 00:08:06.633
What can I do?

00:08:06.633 --> 00:08:08.739
The guy's supposed to have
become a heroine addict.

00:08:08.739 --> 00:08:10.047
Okay, well, so what do I do

00:08:10.047 --> 00:08:12.791
to make that seem like it happened?

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:15.595
And the only thing I
could come up with was

00:08:15.595 --> 00:08:17.418
to lose as much weight as I could,

00:08:17.418 --> 00:08:19.304
and then put it back on as fast as I could

00:08:19.304 --> 00:08:21.014
to go do the flashback stuff.

00:08:21.014 --> 00:08:22.274
And so that's what I did.

00:08:22.274 --> 00:08:23.793
- I heard that wasn't
good for your health.

00:08:23.793 --> 00:08:24.721
Like your doctor was surprised.

00:08:24.721 --> 00:08:26.471
- No it was terrible.

00:08:27.596 --> 00:08:30.557
It was bad because I didn't, I asked them

00:08:30.557 --> 00:08:34.724
for a nutritionist, which
was probably $1500 or $2500,

00:08:36.609 --> 00:08:38.498
and they said no.

00:08:38.498 --> 00:08:41.045
I don't think they, in their defense,

00:08:41.045 --> 00:08:44.892
I don't think they really
knew what I was going to do.

00:08:44.892 --> 00:08:47.027
They probably have requests
like this all the time,

00:08:47.027 --> 00:08:48.272
and they think they're vanity requests,

00:08:48.272 --> 00:08:51.735
but it was a serious request
and they turned it down.

00:08:51.735 --> 00:08:53.781
And so I went to a friend.

00:08:53.781 --> 00:08:55.657
We had a friend. We knew a guy--

00:08:55.657 --> 00:08:58.049
(laughing)

00:08:58.049 --> 00:09:01.116
who was also, he was Austrian.

00:09:01.116 --> 00:09:03.169
I mean, funnily enough, he was Austrian

00:09:03.169 --> 00:09:05.293
and he was trying to be an actor

00:09:05.293 --> 00:09:07.165
but he literally, because he was Austrian,

00:09:07.165 --> 00:09:11.448
he had Arnold's accent and
he was a former bodybuilder.

00:09:11.448 --> 00:09:15.232
So he was really aiming
at a small bullseye,

00:09:15.232 --> 00:09:16.247
(laughing)

00:09:16.247 --> 00:09:20.358
because his spot was
really taken by somebody.

00:09:20.358 --> 00:09:22.691
But he put me on his program

00:09:24.339 --> 00:09:26.690
that he would do for bodybuilding shows.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:29.427
But they would do that
program three weeks out.

00:09:29.427 --> 00:09:33.510
They would do this really
kind of reckless thing,

00:09:34.471 --> 00:09:36.745
and so those guys walk on stage

00:09:36.745 --> 00:09:37.951
and you could push, they look strong,

00:09:37.951 --> 00:09:39.231
but you could knock them over.

00:09:39.231 --> 00:09:42.016
They're really suffering at that point.

00:09:42.016 --> 00:09:44.679
To kind of leach every
bit of everything out

00:09:44.679 --> 00:09:47.068
so that the veins and the muscles pop out.

00:09:47.068 --> 00:09:50.728
So I did it for like three
and a half or four months,

00:09:50.728 --> 00:09:53.561
which was just too much, too much.

00:09:54.554 --> 00:09:57.221
But at the same time, it worked.

00:09:59.205 --> 00:10:03.201
It worked, and when I got The
Rainmaker a year or so later,

00:10:03.201 --> 00:10:06.160
Coppola said that he'd
seen Courage Under Fire,

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.512
and that that made a big difference.

00:10:08.512 --> 00:10:10.649
And funnily enough it
was Edward Norton and I

00:10:10.649 --> 00:10:13.871
who were going against
each other again for that,

00:10:13.871 --> 00:10:17.086
and the Courage Under Fire
pushed me over the edge.

00:10:17.086 --> 00:10:21.253
And when I met Spielberg
later, and he looked at me,

00:10:22.206 --> 00:10:23.522
and he said, "What?"

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:26.001
And I'd put myself on tape
for Saving Private Ryan.

00:10:26.001 --> 00:10:26.908
I never heard anything.

00:10:26.908 --> 00:10:29.047
I don't think the tape every got to him.

00:10:29.047 --> 00:10:33.145
The casting director maybe
looked at it and chucked it.

00:10:33.145 --> 00:10:35.465
So I thought he'd seen it.

00:10:35.465 --> 00:10:37.072
And he said, "What do I know you from?"

00:10:37.072 --> 00:10:38.943
And I said, "I put myself
on tape for your movie."

00:10:38.943 --> 00:10:40.590
He goes, "Nah, I didn't see any tape."

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:41.582
He goes, "What movies have you been in?"

00:10:41.582 --> 00:10:43.508
I said, "I was in a movie
called Courage Under Fire."

00:10:43.508 --> 00:10:46.682
And he goes, "You know I turned to my wife

00:10:46.682 --> 00:10:47.837
when I saw that movie and said

00:10:47.837 --> 00:10:50.097
that's the exact guy I
want for Private Ryan.

00:10:50.097 --> 00:10:51.983
I just wish he wasn't so skinny."

00:10:51.983 --> 00:10:54.233
(laughter)

00:10:56.319 --> 00:10:58.761
- I feel like I read a
interview at the time

00:10:58.761 --> 00:11:00.731
that said you couldn't
even kiss your girlfriend

00:11:00.731 --> 00:11:03.308
because you could taste
potato chips on her lips.

00:11:03.308 --> 00:11:05.475
- The oil from them, yeah.

00:11:06.993 --> 00:11:10.277
People who have those disorders, I got it.

00:11:10.277 --> 00:11:12.277
I totally understood it.

00:11:13.602 --> 00:11:16.813
I just told myself I can't allow anything,

00:11:16.813 --> 00:11:19.620
there's no, no compromising.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:23.287
None, because the second
you open that door,

00:11:24.232 --> 00:11:25.812
it's a slippery slope.

00:11:25.812 --> 00:11:27.019
I wanted to look back on it

00:11:27.019 --> 00:11:29.862
and go, "I did absolutely
everything I could."

00:11:29.862 --> 00:11:32.646
- I had been working my whole life,

00:11:32.646 --> 00:11:33.891
and what I didn't understand

00:11:33.891 --> 00:11:35.831
by being determined to taste something,

00:11:35.831 --> 00:11:36.978
by being committed to it.

00:11:36.978 --> 00:11:38.041
And what commitment is,

00:11:38.041 --> 00:11:39.053
commitment is staying true to

00:11:39.053 --> 00:11:40.373
what you said you were going to do long

00:11:40.373 --> 00:11:42.539
after the mood that you
have said it in has left.

00:11:42.539 --> 00:11:43.908
You see, people think
commitment is saying,

00:11:43.908 --> 00:11:46.890
"Yes, I'll do it on the
days when it feel good."

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:47.973
But I have been committed to everything

00:11:47.973 --> 00:11:49.381
that I have ever started in my life,

00:11:49.381 --> 00:11:50.973
and I never stopped, and I never quitted.

00:11:50.973 --> 00:11:53.402
And so by being committed to
everything that I started,

00:11:53.402 --> 00:11:55.904
I finished it. It built
the certain type of spirit.

00:11:55.904 --> 00:11:57.682
It built the certain type of mentality.

00:11:57.682 --> 00:11:59.580
It built the certain type of individual.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:02.225
And so now I couldn't
quit even if I wanted to.

00:12:02.225 --> 00:12:04.355
I couldn't lay in the
bed even if I wanted to.

00:12:04.355 --> 00:12:06.522
I couldn't stop even if I wanted to.

00:12:06.522 --> 00:12:08.839
I have too much sweat equity in my life,

00:12:08.839 --> 00:12:10.730
in everything that I was doing.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:14.122
Because I understood my
existence wasn't about me.

00:12:14.122 --> 00:12:16.306
I went from me to we a long time ago.

00:12:16.306 --> 00:12:19.328
I understood the process is
more important than the product.

00:12:19.328 --> 00:12:21.076
It wasn't about the outcome for me.

00:12:21.076 --> 00:12:22.785
Whether I made it to the NFL or not,

00:12:22.785 --> 00:12:25.063
that was inconsequential
in God's plan for my life.

00:12:25.063 --> 00:12:27.523
But I was going to fall
in love with that process,

00:12:27.523 --> 00:12:29.898
because I understood by falling
in love with that process,

00:12:29.898 --> 00:12:32.044
it was going to turn me into a machine.

